<p>King Charles III and Queen Camilla are due to begin a four-day state visit to the United States on Monday, with both London and Washington casting the trip as a way to honor the long-running UK-US partnership and, potentially, ease recent political friction. The visit will be Charles&#x27;s first state visit to the US as monarch, and the articles say it comes at the request of the British government and Mr Trump as tensions have grown over the Iran war and other bilateral disputes. President Trump told the BBC that the King&#x27;s visit could &quot;absolutely&quot; help repair relations, signaling hope that royal diplomacy can create a friendlier atmosphere even as policy disagreements remain. Across the sources, the trip comes across as both ceremonial and strategic: a symbolic celebration of historic ties and a careful effort to steady the so-called special relationship at a strained moment.</p><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>BBC interview: In a telephone interview broadcast by the BBC, President Trump discussed the King&#x27;s visit, his relationship with UK Prime Minister Keir Starmer, and the war with Iran as part of a broader conversation about transatlantic ties.</li><li>Anniversary frame: Buckingham Palace and the British government have tied the trip in part to 250 years of US independence, giving the visit a celebratory backdrop alongside its diplomatic purpose.</li><li>Royal role: The Christian Science Monitor described the trip as a delicate mission for King Charles, who is expected to use the monarchy&#x27;s soft-power appeal to reinforce the &quot;special relationship&quot; rather than negotiate policy himself.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Donald Trump: He said the King&#x27;s state visit could help mend relations with Britain and spoke positively about the trip&#x27;s potential to improve the bilateral atmosphere. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cx2wdegnzzjo'>BBC</a>)</li><li>British government: Reports describe the visit as coming at the British government&#x27;s request during a difficult stretch in UK-US relations. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/king-charles-to-visit-us-as-political-ties-fray-under-trump'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Buckingham Palace: The palace has presented the four-day trip as a ceremony-led affirmation of the longstanding relationship between the two countries as the US approaches its 250th year of independence. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3351216/trump-says-king-charles-visit-could-absolutely-repair-us-uk-ties'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Christian Science Monitor analysis: Its essay argues that the monarch faces a careful balancing act, using symbolism and continuity to steady a strained alliance without stepping openly into partisan politics. (<a href='https://www.csmonitor.com/Perspectives/Essays/2026/0423/king-charles-trump-white-house-visit'>The Christian Science Monitor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/king-charles-to-visit-us-as-political-ties-fray-under-trump'>King Charles to visit US as political ties fray under Trump</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/04/23/days-before-king-charles-s-state-visit-trump-says-it-could-help-mend-ties-with-london'>Days before King Charles&#x27;s state visit, Trump says it could help mend ties with London</a> - mercopress.com</li><li><a href='https://www.csmonitor.com/Perspectives/Essays/2026/0423/king-charles-trump-white-house-visit'>King Charles III is headed to Washington. Can he steady the ‘special relationship’﻿?</a> - csmonitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cx2wdegnzzjo'>Trump tells BBC that King&#x27;s visit could &#x27;absolutely&#x27; help repair relations with UK</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3351216/trump-says-king-charles-visit-could-absolutely-repair-us-uk-ties'>Trump says King Charles’ visit could ‘absolutely’ repair US-UK ties</a> - scmp.com</li></ul>